  "predictive_services_discussion": "Widespread elevated to critical conditions will persist across portions of the Southwest, Great Basin, and Rocky Mountain areas, as well as central California valleys today. Across the Southwest, Great Basin, and Rocky Mountain areas, mostly westerly winds 15-25 mph with gusts 30-45 mph and relative humidity values between 5-20% are expected, with the highest winds expected across the Front Range in Colorado and large portions of central Wyoming, where gusts may exceed 50 mph in some areas. Across central California valleys, Las Vegas, and southern portions of the Southwest, temperatures between 95-105 degrees are expected in conjunction with relative humidity values below 15% and wind gusts between 15-30 mph. In the northern Rockies, widespread rain with high elevation snow will continue to move east across northern Idaho, northern Wyoming, and large portions of Montana accompanied by high relative humidity values and breezy west winds with gusts of up to 40 mph, which will extend into southeastern Idaho where gusts may exceed 50 mph. In the eastern U.S., scattered showers and thunderstorms will continue to move east across the Midwest and Northeast. Widespread, higher amounts of precipitation are expected across the entire Eastern Area, bringing relative humidity values along the coast to at least 45%. In Alaska, warmer and drier conditions are expected across central Alaska, where relative humidity values below 25% are expected. Scattered light showers will persist across southeastern Alaska today. National Predictive Services Outlook (7-Day Significant Fire Potential Outlook) National Weather Service, Storm Prediction Center: Fire Weather Outlook Map and discussion National Weather Service: Fire Weather Hazards Map National Weather Service, Weather Prediction Center: National Forecast Chart and Short Range Forecast Discussion 6 Minutes for Safety topics can be found here.",
